1
00:00:03,401 --> 00:00:19,030
A pantry wall for the Brooks family: three 24" tall pantries between two tall end panels.

2
00:00:19,030 --> 00:00:27,241
First a tall end panel for the left end...

3
00:00:27,241 --> 00:00:52,421
...then the Tall 24" x 84" pantry preset, three times...

4
00:00:52,421 --> 00:01:05,401
...and a second end panel for the right end.

5
00:01:05,401 --> 00:01:28,000
The wall is 76" wide. Set the room, then Arrange.

6
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:43,068
Arranged along the back wall, end panel to end panel. Plan view shows the fit.

7
00:01:43,068 --> 00:01:50,375
The run is a little short of the wall. This time, split the gap: a filler at each end.

8
00:01:50,375 --> 00:01:52,979
Now the run is centred on the wall, with two equal fillers scribed to the walls.

9
00:01:52,979 --> 00:01:57,437
Elevation: all three pantries and the end panels top out at 84".

10
00:01:57,437 --> 00:02:03,606
Open a pantry to set it up for food storage: more shelves.

11
00:02:03,606 --> 00:02:09,915
Five adjustable shelves on the 32 mm system rows, instead of the preset's count.

12
00:02:09,915 --> 00:02:17,386
Its doors hang on Salice hinges with 3 mm plates; the hinge boring is set here.

13
00:02:17,386 --> 00:02:26,005
Cut list: the tall sides, the shelves, the end panels and the two fillers.

14
00:02:26,005 --> 00:02:33,734
Nesting: every part on 5 x 12 ft sheets, one material per sheet. Sheet 2 holds the backs.

15
00:02:33,734 --> 00:02:39,752
Labels and sheet maps are ready on the Output tab. Machine output switches stay off.

16
00:02:39,752 --> 00:02:42,754
A floor-to-84" pantry wall, centred on its wall with a filler at each end.
